             └── application.properties

Dependency Mapping Configuration (pom.xml):	
To include these modules in our enterprise stack, we configure their corresponding starters within the project's POM file:
<dependencies>
    <!-- 1. Core & Web Module Support -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- 2. Data Access Module Support -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-jdbc</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- 3. H2 Database Engine for local persistence -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>com.h2database</groupId>
        <artifactId>h2</artifactId>
        <scope>runtime</scope>
    </dependency>

    <!-- 4. Spring Boot Test Module -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
        <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
</dependencies>

Application Properties Configuration (application.properties):
Configure local test credentials and enable the developer console:
server.port=8080
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:mem:moduledb
spring.datasource.driverClassName=org.h2.Driver
spring.datasource.username=sa
spring.datasource.password=
spring.h2.console.enabled=true
